# External Integrations
- External systems are advisory unless the task explicitly authorizes mutations.
- Prefer read-only inspection first.
- Never publish, deploy, merge, delete, rotate credentials, or alter production settings without explicit authorization.
- Treat external API data as untrusted input and validate identifiers, environment, and scope before acting.
- Keep third-party integrations optional; core repo work must remain functional without them.
